From 020f50698af62fd76d251cee84e91c981f6ef07c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dandysuper <a@b.c>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 16:40:15 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] a51: Exclude the fingerprint HAL during bring-up

HOLD. Apply only if the fingerprint service fails to build.

fingerprint/Android.bp links android.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint-V4-ndk
and android.hardware.biometrics.common-V4-ndk, and the vintf fragment
declares <version>4</version>. If Android 17 froze V5 and the matrix demands
it, Fingerprint.cpp and Session.cpp must be rebuilt against the new
interface, with stubs for any methods V5 added. Upstream
hardware/samsung/aidl/fingerprint is also still on V4, so there is no
reference implementation to copy - this is not a single-iteration fix.

Excluding the service costs the fingerprint sensor and nothing else. The
device boots, every other subsystem can be validated, and the HAL is
restored by reverting this patch once the AIDL question is resolved.

Note AOSP keeps frozen AIDL versions available indefinitely, so -V4-ndk
should still exist in an Android 17 tree. The risk is a matrix minimum, not
a missing library - try building unmodified first.
---
 device.mk | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/device.mk b/device.mk
index 0cc9a65..dc6102e 100644
--- a/device.mk
+++ b/device.mk
@@ -35,8 +35,13 @@ PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
     fingerprint_common.rc
 
 # Fingerprint
+# HOLD-PATCH 0012: the fingerprint HAL is excluded for bring-up. Its
+# Android.bp pins android.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint-V4-ndk and
+# .common-V4-ndk; if Android 17 requires V5, Fingerprint.cpp and Session.cpp
+# need rebuilding against the new interface, which is not a one-run fix.
+# Dropping the service loses the fingerprint sensor and nothing else - the
+# device boots, and the HAL can be restored once the AIDL version is settled.
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
-    android.hardware.biometrics.fingerprint-service.a51 \
     sensors.samsung
 
 PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \
-- 
